sam.frontend: Hit a reproducible streaming issue on iOS WKWebView during the mobile onboarding test. Chunks get split mid-utf8 and the client JSON parser throws, then on reconnect we sometimes see duplicate final punctuation.

sam.frontend: Repro steps: open demo on iPhone Safari embedded in our app (WKWebView), start stream, flip airplane mode for ~3s, reopen. Happens ~60% of tries.

sam.frontend: App log snippet: 

sam.frontend: ```
[stream] recv: "{\"seq\":45, \"token\":\"I love \\uD83D\""
[stream] recv: "\"DEVELOPERS\\\"}"
[parser] JSON.parse error: Unexpected token D in JSON at position 28
[client] appended: I love \\uD83D
[client] reconnect, last-id=none
[stream] recv: "{\"seq\":46, \"token\":\"!\"}"
[client] appended: DEVELOPERS}
[client] final: I love \\uD83DDEVELOPERS} !
```

lee.sdk: looks like the surrogate pair for the emoji got split. many JSON parsers choke if you feed incomplete UTF-8 sequences into JSON.parse.

nina: which SDK are you running? JS browser or our embedded mobile SDK shim?

sam.frontend: It's the in-app WKWebView running our web UI (so browser JS). We also saw different behaviour when testing with the EventSource polyfill vs native EventSource.

lee.sdk: parity note: our Swift SDK (mobile) uses a byte-assembly approach that buffers until valid UTF-8 boundary then decodes -> no error. Browser path was optimistic and parsed each event line. gap.

chris.runtime: can we add SSE-level ids (Last-Event-ID) from the runtime and a per-token seq in payload so clients can dedupe on resume? Also could add retry: and a small heartbeat to keep connections alive on mobile.

sam.frontend: Adding SSE id would help resume, but doesn't prevent mid-packet parse errors. We need client buffering + robust UTF-8 handling.

lee.sdk: propose a small helper lib in devex: stream-safe-parse. responsibilities: incremental utf8-decoding, newline/json-stream framing, optional reassembly by seq, and Last-Event-ID resume helper. We can ship small UMD + ESM and include in sample-app.

nina: +1. for immediate fix in the workshop, can you switch the demo to use fetch+reader with TextDecoder streaming (it can handle partial utf8) and wait for newline delim? Example: 

nina: ```js
const r = await fetch('/v1/streams?session=xyz');
const reader = r.body.getReader();
const decoder = new TextDecoder();
let buf = '';
while(true){
  const {done, value} = await reader.read();
  if(done) break;
  buf += decoder.decode(value, {stream: true});
  let i;
  while((i = buf.indexOf('\n')) !== -1){
    const line = buf.slice(0,i).trim();
    buf = buf.slice(i+1);
    if(!line) continue;
    // safe parse: line should be full JSON
    appendToken(JSON.parse(line).token);
  }
}
```

lee.sdk: add unit tests: simulate 3-byte and 4-byte utf8 split across read() boundaries, plus newline-less JSON fragments. verify stream-safe-parse doesn't throw and emits tokens in order.

chris.runtime: ENG-STREAM-519 opened to track: (A) runtime: emit SSE id headers and optional retry, (B) devex: ship stream-safe-parse lib and update sample-app, (C) docs: best-practices for mobile/wkwebview, (D) tests for polyfill vs native parity.

sam.frontend: thanks. i'll try the fetch+decoder patch now and test on device lab. will report back with canary results.

devbot: Note: demo cluster reported higher EOF rates at 2026-03-24T09:11Z; linked ENG-STREAM-519.

lee.sdk: also add a small troubleshooting note: if you see duplicated final tokens after reconnect, check Last-Event-ID headers and server seq ids; client should only apply messages with seq > last_applied_seq.

nina: i'll add a short section in the onboarding doc and the workshop slides pointing to the new helper and the SDK parity checklist.

sam.frontend: great, i'll validate on devices and update this thread.
